comments.body:
2026-09-04 user self-test FAILED the product milestone despite prior movement-only runtime PASS.

Observed player-visible failures in the normal human launch path:
- placeholder/dummy pawn floating; no useful animation, jump, camera scroll/shoulder swap, or character roster switching;
- production world appeared flat/empty: no readable road/lane/base/core/creep battle, no asset dressing/grass/wind/time-of-day;
- no visible grapple, meteor/spells/skills, earthworks, mounts/flying, or asset-ring/showcase behavior;
- two flapping birds were untextured; Asylum Demon appeared giant/sideways/out-of-map;
- Shift did not present Tribes-style skiing.

Runtime log corroboration: repeated `P3_LANEWAR_CREEP_PRESENTATION ... QUALIFIED=0 MESH=0 LOCOMOTION=0 MELEE=0 DAMAGE=0 DEFEAT=0` for ordinary, raptor, hummingbird and jellyfish enemies, plus repeated unloadable Tiny3D skeletal mesh/locomotion/attack/hit/death packages. This means subsystem/source presence was being counted while required player-visible runtime assets and bindings were absent.

#803 remains the existing convergence owner; do not create another vertical-slice system. Acceptance is now explicitly the HUMAN launcher, not a movement-only PIE probe. Before calling #803 testable again, the same normal launch must visibly prove: real animated selectable character, jump/camera/shoulder swap, grapple + real skiing, spells including meteor, earthworks, two bases/core/road/lane, visible qualified creeps, environment dressing/grass/wind/time-of-day, flying/mount path, and readable destruction/construction. Missing/unloadable runtime dependencies are product failures, not optional proof hydration.
